    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0037" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890H.24/86: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-27T10:00:00+04:00">May 27, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 28—11:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>109. Your 45, April 15.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d23-f1"/> Please inform the War
                    Department that on May 17 the Military Attaché and I officially presented the
                    Dodge army station wagon intended for the King,<anchor n="9" xml:id="d23-f2"/>
                    and on May 25 we presented the Stearman trainer plane intended for the Afghan
                    Air Force. See my telegram 78, September 20, 1942.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d23-f3"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Both gifts were highly appreciated and I have been requested to convey to the
                    Government of the United States and to the authorities directly concerned the
                    sincere thanks of the Afghan Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
